    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA well-presented two-bedroom semi-detached residence located in a quiet cul-de-sac within the popular Renville Village development, a mature and well-maintained coastal setting on the outskirts of Oranmore. No. 72A enjoys a private position within the development and offers bright, comfortable accommodation, off-street parking and a larger-than-typical rear garden for the estate.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance porch, entrance hall, guest WC, kitchen and an open-plan dining/living area. A ground floor double bedroom with ensuite provides excellent flexibility and convenience, while the property is presented in good condition throughout and is ready for immediate occupation.\n\nUpstairs, there is a spacious double bedroom with ensuite together with a large hot press providing valuable storage space. The layout is practical and well suited to a range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, downsizers and those seeking a holiday home in a highly sought-after location.\n\nTo the front, the property benefits from private off-street parking. The rear garden is larger than those typically associated with the development, providing excellent outdoor space for relaxing, gardening or entertaining while enjoying the privacy of this quiet cul-de-sac setting.\n\nRenville Village enjoys an enviable location close to the recently rebranded Hawthorn Hotel & Golf Resort, Galway Bay Sailing Club and the scenic walks of Renville Park. Oranmore Village is just a short drive away, offering an excellent range of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, public transport links and easy access to Galway City."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nTiled floor in porch, semi solid timber floor in hall, storage closet, under stairs storage, carpet on stairs, side aspect window in porch.\n\nLiving Dining Room: - \nSemi solid timber floor, open fire, raised hearth, front aspect window.\n\nKitchen: - \nTiled floor, wall & floor kitchen units, tiled splashback, plumbed for washing machine, Indesit hob, Candy oven.\n\nBedroom 1 (Ground Floor): - \nSemi solid timber floor, front aspect window.\n\nEn Suite: - \nTiled floor & shower, wc, wash hand basin, mirror & light, shower unit.\n\nWC: - \nSemi solid timber floor, wc, wash hand basin, mirror.\n\nHot Press: - \nShelved, hot water tank.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nCarpet on floor, built in wardrobe, front aspect window.\n\nEn Suite: - \nTiled floor & shower, wc, wash hand basin, mirror & light, shower unit.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Quiet cul-de-sac location</li><li>Larger-than-average rear garden</li><li>Two ensuite bedrooms</li><li>Off-street parking</li><li>Excellent coastal setting near Renville Park, Hawthorn Golf Resort & Galway Bay Sailing Club</li><li>Ocean Property Mgt Service fee approx. 900 per annum</ul>"
      },
